  "id": "Compound::DB00728 - Gene::1140",
  "verbalization": "Ruronium is linked to Chrnb1 through a series of molecular interactions that involve neuromuscular blockade and receptor antagonism. The evidence suggests that Rocuronium, as part of the Neuromuscular Nondepolarizing Blockade class, binds to Chrnb1, with the lowest common ancestor of Rocuronium and its related compounds (Pancuronium, Pipecuronium) pointing to Nicotinic Antagonist and Steroid Ester pathways. This implies that Rocuronium's mechanism of action is mediated through a shared structural or functional relationship with other neuromuscular blockers, ultimately leading to a binding event with Chrnb1. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Chrnb1, including both nicotinic antagonism and steroid ester interactions, suggests a complex, multi-faceted mechanism by which Rocuronium influences the function of Chrnb1. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering both receptor-target interactions and broader pharmacological contexts in understanding the molecular basis of Rocuronium's effects.",
